          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do I make sealed stamped concrete less slippery?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Mix an anti-slip additive into the final coat, keep coats thin to preserve texture, and choose a satin or semi-gloss sheen instead of high gloss. If an older patio is already slick from buildup, partially stripping and applying one fresh coat with grit can restore traction."
          }
